 r"I am writing to apply for the Data Insights Analyst position in the Data Science \& Analytics team at Howden UK\&I. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have analysed customer and health data, built dashboards that teams use to track performance, and explained the results to people who are not analysts.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the analysis has a visible end point: insight into customer behaviour and market performance that helps product teams improve health insurance for their customers. The posting's focus on the health insurance market is a natural fit for my background in health data, and its emphasis on storytelling and stakeholder partnership matches the part of analytics I enjoy most. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse large merchant and transaction datasets in SQL and Python to find the drivers behind performance across the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Much of the work is helping stakeholders agree what a KPI should measure before building anything, and the recurring lesson has been that the first metric someone asks for is rarely the one that answers their question. I also used Claude Code to automate a repetitive campaign configuration task, which cut the time it took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern for a pharmaceutical client. I built a pipeline that turned more than 4,800 free-text patient consultation threads into structured data for analysis, and I presented findings, risks and recommendations to clinical and business stakeholders. This taught me to translate detailed analysis into a few clear points that a decision-maker can act on.",

